  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa Regional: High-Level Regional Conference on Land and Conflict in the East and Horn of Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Experts drawn from representatives of the Member States of the Intergovernmental Authority on Development (IGAD), the African Union, the United Nations system and other international organizations, think tanks, academia, civil society organizations, and the private sector.
Indirect beneficiaries: Population of East Africa, particularly women and girls, and parties to land conflicts.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to explore the linkages between access to justice and the rule of law, peace, sustainable development and climate change and to contribute towards the achievement of the High-Level Regional Conference on Land and Conflict in the East and Horn of Africa in October 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
